    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0596" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg502"/>

                <head>No. 332.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 28, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d332-f1"/> of the 20th of May last, I have the honor to transmit to
                    you herewith copy of a report by the minister of justice of the Dominion of
                    Canada upon the seizure of the American fishing vessel <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >David J. Adams</hi>, which I am instructed by Her Majesty’s principal
                    secretary of state for foreign affairs to communicate to the United States
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d332-a1.xml" xpointer="d332-a1"/>
